Leonix
======

Leonix is a kernel for the Arduino Leonardo (ATmega32U4), written in C
and AVR assembly and built with avr-gcc.  It does not use the Arduino
core or any of its libraries.

The board is meant to run on its own, powered from the barrel jack or
VIN, with no host computer attached.  The USB port is used only for
flashing.

A Chinese version of this file is in README.zh_CN.


Status
------

Nothing builds yet.  The tree currently holds the notes that the start
code will be written against.


Hardware
--------

  - Arduino Leonardo (A000057): ATmega32U4 at 16 MHz, 32 KiB flash of
    which 28 KiB is left to the application by the Caterina
    bootloader, 2.5 KiB SRAM, 1 KiB EEPROM.
  - Planned console: an HD44780 character LCD behind a PCF8574 I2C
    expander.


Toolchain
---------

  - avr-gcc (developed with 9.5.0) and binutils for AVR
  - avrdude, talking AVR109 to the Caterina bootloader

The Caterina bootloader is entered only by pressing the reset button,
because Leonix has no USB CDC port to receive the 1200 baud reset.
Documentation/booting.rst, section 5, has the details.


Documentation
-------------

Documentation/booting.rst
	The machine state the Caterina bootloader leaves behind when it
	jumps to the application, and what the start code has to undo.

Documentation/references/index.rst
	Every datasheet and external source the project relies on, with
	document number and revision.

Only the Leonardo schematic is shipped in the tree, because it is the
only reference released under a licence that allows redistribution
(CC BY-SA 4.0).  The other datasheets have to be fetched separately:

	cd Documentation/references
	curl -L -o ATmega16U4-32U4-datasheet-7766J.pdf \
	  https://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/en/DeviceDoc/Atmel-7766-8-bit-AVR-ATmega16U4-32U4_Datasheet.pdf
	curl -L -o AVR-InstructionSet-Manual-DS40002198.pdf \
	  https://ww1.microchip.com/downloads/aemDocuments/documents/MCU08/ProductDocuments/ReferenceManuals/AVR-InstructionSet-Manual-DS40002198.pdf
	curl -L -o HD44780U-Hitachi.pdf \
	  https://cdn.sparkfun.com/assets/9/5/f/7/b/HD44780.pdf
	curl -L -o PCF8574-TI.pdf \
	  https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/pcf8574.pdf

These files are not covered by .gitignore.  Add their names to
.git/info/exclude so they are not committed by accident.


Licence
-------

No licence has been chosen for the Leonix sources yet.  The Leonardo
schematic in Documentation/references is Arduino's work, distributed
under CC BY-SA 4.0.
